<%# Student trading: the state as a sentence, with its control on the same line.

    Three arrangements in, and the previous two were both wrong in the same direction - inventing a
    shape rather than using the system.

      1. A bare switch labelled "Trading" in the page header's action area, beside "Add student". A
         setting is not a page action, and the state was carried by the track's colour alone.
      2. Its own card, with a status pill sitting to the *left* of the sentence and the switch
         labelled with a verb ("Turn off"). No design system puts a pill inline before body text:
         Polaris, Primer and Carbon all place one against a title or on its own line. It was also the
         third copy of one fact - pill, sentence, and switch position all said on or off - and
         Polaris's verb belongs on a *button*, not on a switch, so "Turn on" beside a pill reading
         "Trading off" gave the reader two things to reconcile.

    So: no pill, and the label is the noun. A switch's position is its state, which is the whole
    convention - iOS, Material and Polaris all pair a noun with a switch and never a verb - and the
    sentence beside it says the state in words for anyone who should not have to read a control. The
    consequence follows in the same sentence, because that is the thing a teacher is actually deciding.

    No card of its own either. It sits in the Students section, on the line under the heading, which is
    where a section's control goes in Polaris (card header action), Primer (Subhead) and Stripe. That
    took the page from six surfaces to two. %>
<% on = classroom.trading_enabled? %>

<div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
  <p class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
    <span class="font-medium text-slate-900">
      <%= on ? "Trading is on." : "Trading is off." %>
    </span>
    <% if on %>
      Students can buy and sell shares. Turning this off stops new orders - it does not sell anything
      they already hold.
    <% else %>
      Students cannot buy or sell, and they see a note explaining why. Nothing they already hold is
      affected.<% if classroom.trading_disabled_at.present? %>
        Off since <%= l(classroom.trading_disabled_at.to_date, format: :long) %>.<% end %>
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <%= form_with url: toggle_trading_classroom_path(classroom), method: :patch, class: "contents" do %>
    <label class="inline-flex shrink-0 cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
      <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 select-none">Trading</span>
      <%= check_box_tag "trading", "1", on,
                        class: "peer sr-only",
                        disabled: !policy(classroom).toggle_trading?,
                        data: { controller: "submit-on-change",
                                action: "change->submit-on-change#submit" } %>
      <%# The track needs 3:1 against the page as a UI boundary: green-700 is 4.79:1 checked,
          slate-400 is 2.9:1 unchecked, so the unchecked track also carries a border. %>
      <div class="peer relative h-5 w-9 rounded-full border border-slate-400 bg-slate-300 after:absolute after:top-0.5 after:start-0.5 after:h-4 after:w-4 after:rounded-full after:bg-white after:transition-all after:content-[''] peer-checked:border-green-700 peer-checked:bg-green-700 peer-checked:after:translate-x-full rtl:peer-checked:after:-translate-x-full"></div>
    </label>
  <% end %>
</div>
